Ordenar_articulo.py
====================

Reformats an academic article (.docx) according to the “clean” reference format:

    Title[es]:...
    Title[en]:...
    Title[pt]:...                (if applicable)
    Author 1¹ https://orcid.org/xxxx
    Author 2¹ https://orcid.org/xxxx
    ¹Affiliation
    email1
    email2
    SUMMARY
    <text>
    Keywords: ...
    ABSTRACT
    <text>
    Keywords: ...
    SUMMARY                       (if applicable)
    <text>
    Keywords: ...
    date-rec: YYYY-MM-DD
    date-acc: YYYY-MM-DD
    date-pub: YYYY-MM-DD
    section:INTRODUCTION
    ...
    section:METHODS
    ...
    section:RESULTS...
    ...
    section:DISCUSSION
    ...
    section:CONCLUSIONS
    ...
    REFERENCES
    ...

The body of the document (introduction, methods, results, discussion,
conclusions, tables, references) is NOT rewritten: it is preserved exactly as
it appears in the original .docx file (including tables, italics, symbols, etc.), with only
the “section:” labels prepended to the main headings.

USAGE
---
    python3 sort_article.py input.docx output.docx

If certain data is not detected correctly automatically (titles, authors,
affiliations, etc.), edit the MANUAL_OVERRIDE section below to force
those values instead of relying on automatic detection.
